## 1. System Overview

The ExaDigiT cooling model is a high-fidelity Modelica-based digital twin of the ORNL Frontier supercomputer liquid cooling system. It models the complete thermal chain from individual silicon chips to the atmosphere, enabling end-to-end simulation of energy consumption and thermal performance.

### 1.1 Full Thermal Chain

```
CHIP (Silicon, 3D conduction)
  ↓  chip heat conducted to cold plate surface
COLD PLATE (SS316, conjugate heat transfer)
  ↓  coolant carries heat from server
CDU HEAT EXCHANGER (counter-flow, 5-node, empirical UA table)
  ↓  building water carries heat from CDU
HOT WATER LOOP (EHX, 4 pump trains, 4 HX trains)
  ↓  inner loop water carries heat to cooling tower
COOLING TOWER (York correlation, evaporative rejection)
  ↓  heat rejected to atmosphere
ATMOSPHERE (wet bulb temperature boundary condition)
```

> **Source:** Chain derived by tracing `connect()` statements across:
> - `Models/v1.mo` — top-level assembly connecting datacenter to centralEnergyPlant
> - `Systems/CentralEnergyPlant/Models/v0.mo` — connecting hotWaterLoop to coolingTowerLoop
> - `Systems/Datacenter/Systems/CoolingBlock/Models/v0.mo` — connecting CDU to cabinet
> - `Components/SubComponents/DataCenter/Blade/Blade_coldplates.mo` — connecting chip to cold plate

### 1.2 Two Datacenter Zones

The model supports two datacenter zones connected to one central energy plant:

```modelica
replaceable Systems.Datacenter.Models.v0 datacenter[structure.datacenter.n_int]
replaceable Systems.Datacenter.Models.v0 datacenter_1[structure.datacenter_1.n_int]
```

> **Source:** `Models/v1.mo` — lines declaring `datacenter` and `datacenter_1` as separate array instances

### 1.3 Plenum Mixing Volumes (Top Level)

Two mixing volumes act as fluid manifolds connecting multiple datacenters to one central plant:

```
V_plenum_inlet  = 150 m³   (plenum_inlet_datacenter,  V=300/2)
V_plenum_outlet = 150 m³   (plenum_outlet_datacenter, V=300/2)
```

> **Source:** `Models/v1.mo`:
> ```modelica
> TRANSFORM.Fluid.Volumes.MixingVolume plenum_outlet_datacenter(
>   redeclare model Geometry = ... (V=300/2), ...
> ```

### 1.4 Two Fluid Media (Central Energy Plant)

The system uses two hydraulically separate fluid circuits coupled only by heat exchange:

```
Medium (outer loop):       Datacenter ↔ Hot Water Loop primary side
Medium_inner (inner loop): Hot Water Loop secondary side ↔ Cooling Tower Loop
```

```modelica
replaceable package Medium_inner =
    TRANSFORM.Media.Fluids.Water.LinearWaterHot_pT
```

> **Source:** `Systems/CentralEnergyPlant/Models/v0.mo` — `Medium_inner` declaration. The two media are never mixed — they exchange heat only through the EHX heat exchanger inside the Hot Water Loop.

