## 3. Cold Plate Model
**File:** `Components/SubComponents/Fluid/ColdPlate/coldPlate.mo`

The cold plate is the thermal interface between the chip and the liquid cooling circuit. It models conjugate heat transfer — simultaneous fluid flow and 2D solid wall conduction in stainless steel.

### 3.1 Physical Configuration

```
Chip heat (heatPorts[nZ]) → SS316 wall (2D conduction) → fluid pipe (flow) → coolant out
```

### 3.2 Wall Material

```modelica
replaceable package Material = TRANSFORM.Media.Solids.SS316
```

> **Source:** `coldPlate.mo` — `Material` parameter declaration. SS316 stainless steel is the default wall material with known thermal conductivity, density, and specific heat.

### 3.3 Governing Equations

#### Fluid Energy Balance (at each node along pipe)

```
m · cp · dT/dt = m_flow · cp · (T_in - T_out) + Q_from_wall
```

> **Source:** `coldPlate.mo` — the fluid pipe is `TRANSFORM.Fluid.Pipes.GenericPipe_MultiTransferSurface`. This TRANSFORM component implements the 1D fluid energy balance at each node. The `use_HeatTransfer=true` flag enables wall-to-fluid heat transfer.
> ```modelica
> TRANSFORM.Fluid.Pipes.GenericPipe_MultiTransferSurface pipe(
>     ...
>     use_HeatTransfer=true,
>     redeclare model HeatTransfer = HeatTransfer, ...)
> ```

#### 2D Wall Conduction (SS316)

```
ρ · cp · ∂T/∂t = k · (∂²T/∂r² + ∂²T/∂z²) + Q_gen
```

Where r is radial (wall thickness) and z is axial (along flow).

> **Source:** `coldPlate.mo`:
> ```modelica
> TRANSFORM.HeatAndMassTransfer.DiscritizedModels.Conduction_2D wall(
>   redeclare package Material = Material,
>   redeclare model Geometry =
>       TRANSFORM.Fluid.ClosureRelations.Geometry.Models.DistributedVolume_1D.ShellSide_STHX
>       (r_outer=wall.geometry.r_inner + sum(geometry.ths_wall)/geometry.nV,
>        length_z=sum(geometry.dlengths)), ...)
> ```
> `Conduction_2D` from TRANSFORM solves the 2D heat equation in cylindrical/shell coordinates.

#### Conjugate Coupling (wall → fluid)

```
Q_wall→fluid = h · A · (T_wall_inner - T_fluid)
```

> **Source:** `coldPlate.mo` equation section:
> ```modelica
> connect(wall.port_a1, pipe.heatPorts[:,1])
> ```
> This connects the inner wall surface heat ports to the fluid pipe heat ports at each axial node, enabling convective coupling.

#### Chip → Wall Connection

```modelica
connect(wall.port_b1, heatPorts)
```

> **Source:** `coldPlate.mo` equation section. `heatPorts[geometry.nZ]` is the external interface that receives chip heat from `GPU_3D.port_b` or `CPU_3D.port_b`.

#### Adiabatic End Conditions

```modelica
TRANSFORM.HeatAndMassTransfer.BoundaryConditions.Heat.Adiabatic adiabatic_a[geometry.nR]
TRANSFORM.HeatAndMassTransfer.BoundaryConditions.Heat.Adiabatic adiabatic_b[geometry.nR]
```

> **Source:** `coldPlate.mo` — inlet and outlet end faces of the wall are declared adiabatic. No heat escapes from the ends, only through the chip contact surface.

### 3.4 GPU vs CPU Cold Plate Difference

```modelica
Fluid.ColdPlate.coldPlate coldPlate(use_HeatTransferOuter=true)   -- GPU
Fluid.ColdPlate.coldPlate coldPlate2                               -- CPU (default false)
```

> **Source:** `Blade_coldplates.mo` — GPU cold plate instantiation passes `use_HeatTransferOuter=true`, meaning the outer wall temperature is explicitly solved. CPU cold plates use the default (false), meaning heat flux is prescribed instead.

