## 4. Cabinet Model
**File:** `Systems/Datacenter/Systems/CoolingBlock/Systems/Cabinet/Models/v0.mo`

The cabinet model represents an entire server rack as a single lumped fluid volume. Individual blades are aggregated for computational efficiency.

### 4.1 Physical Configuration

```
port_a → dp_inlet (R_Cab/2) → coolingChannels (fluid volume + heat port) → dp_outlet (R_Cab/2) → port_b
                                        ↑
                              boundary.Q_flow_ext
                                        ↑
                              controlBus.Q_flow  ← WORKLOAD HEAT INPUT
```

### 4.2 Key Parameters

| Parameter | Value | Source Line |
|-----------|-------|-------------|
| R_Cab | 33,000 | `redeclare replaceable Data.v0 data(R_Cab=33000)` |
| dp_inlet resistance | R_Cab × 0.5 | `dp_inlet(... R=data.R_Cab*0.5)` |
| dp_outlet resistance | R_Cab × 0.5 | `dp_outlet(... R=data.R_Cab*0.5)` |
| Fluid volume | data.ccVolCabinet | `coolingChannels(... V=data.ccVolCabinet)` |

> **Source:** `Cabinet/Models/v0.mo` — component declarations and parameter assignments.

### 4.3 Workload Heat Injection — Critical Line

```modelica
connect(controlBus.Q_flow, boundary.Q_flow_ext)
```

> **Source:** `Cabinet/Models/v0.mo` equation section. This single line is where compute workload data enters the physical model. `Q_flow` (watts) represents total electrical power dissipated as heat by all servers in the cabinet. To use real HPC job scheduler data, feed time-series power values into `controlBus.Q_flow`.

### 4.4 Cabinet Energy Balance

```
m · cp · dT/dt = m_flow · cp · (T_in - T_out) + Q_flow
```

> **Source:** `Cabinet/Models/v0.mo`:
> ```modelica
> TRANSFORM.Fluid.Volumes.SimpleVolume coolingChannels(
>     ...
>     use_HeatPort=true)
> TRANSFORM.HeatAndMassTransfer.BoundaryConditions.Heat.HeatFlow boundary(use_port=true)
> connect(boundary.port, coolingChannels.heatPort)
> connect(controlBus.Q_flow, boundary.Q_flow_ext)
> ```
> `SimpleVolume` with `use_HeatPort=true` implements the fluid energy balance. `HeatFlow` boundary injects Q_flow as an external heat source.

