## 6. Cooling Block & Datacenter Assembly
**Files:** `Systems/Datacenter/Systems/CoolingBlock/Models/v0.mo`,
`Systems/Datacenter/Models/v0.mo`

### 6.1 Cooling Block — Two-Loop Separation

The CoolingBlock maintains hydraulic isolation between server coolant and building water, exactly mirroring the Hot Water Loop structure:

```
port_a (building water) → CDU[primary] → port_b
CDU[secondary] ↔ Cabinet (server coolant loop — closed, internal)
```

> **Source:** `CoolingBlock/Models/v0.mo`:
> ```modelica
> connect(cdu.port_b2, plenum_inlet_cabinet.port_a)
> connect(plenum_outlet_cabinet.port_b, cdu.port_a2)
> ```
> CDU secondary outlet feeds cabinet inlet; cabinet outlet returns to CDU secondary inlet — forming a closed server-side loop.

### 6.2 Bypass Valve — Datacenter Level

A bypass valve allows coolant to short-circuit the compute blocks when server load is low:

```modelica
TRANSFORM.Fluid.Valves.ValveLinear valveBypass(
    dp_nominal(displayUnit="Pa") = data.dP_valve_bypass,
    m_flow_nominal=data.bypass_nom_flow)
TRANSFORM.Fluid.FittingsAndResistances.PressureLoss bypassPipe(
    ... dp0=data.dP_bypass)
connect(controlBus.opening_bypass, valveBypass.opening)
```

> **Source:** `Datacenter/Models/v0.mo` — component declarations and control bus connection. Opening the bypass reduces pump back-pressure and saves energy during low-load periods.

### 6.3 Mass Flow Sensor

```modelica
TRANSFORM.Fluid.Sensors.MassFlowRate sensor_m_flow
connect(controlBus.m_flow_supply, sensor_m_flow.m_flow)
```

> **Source:** `Datacenter/Models/v0.mo` — total supply flow is measured and broadcast to the control bus for use by higher-level controllers.

