## 10. Pump Train
**File:** `Components/SubComponents/Fluid/Pumps/PumpTrain.mo`

### 10.1 Physical Configuration

```
port_a → valve (opening) → volume (V=0.01 m³) → pump (N=speed signal) → port_b
```

> **Source:** `PumpTrain.mo` — `connect()` statements:
> ```modelica
> connect(valve.port_b, volume.port_a)
> connect(volume.port_b, pump.port_a)
> connect(valve.port_a, port_a)
> connect(pump.port_b, port_b)
> ```

### 10.2 Buffer Volume

```modelica
TRANSFORM.Fluid.Volumes.SimpleVolume volume(
    ...
    redeclare replaceable model Geometry = ...GenericVolume(V=0.01))
```

> **Source:** `PumpTrain.mo` — volume declaration. V=0.01 m³ provides numerical stability between the valve and pump — represents real pipe volume.

### 10.3 Control Inputs

```modelica
Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput opening  "=1: completely open, =0: completely closed"
Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput N
connect(valve.opening, opening)
connect(pump.inputSignal, N)
```

> **Source:** `PumpTrain.mo` — interface declarations and connect statements.

### 10.4 Pump Affinity Laws

The controlled pump (`TRANSFORM.Fluid.Machines.Pump_Controlled`) implements the centrifugal pump affinity laws:

```
Q_flow ∝ N       (flow proportional to speed)
ΔP     ∝ N²      (head proportional to speed squared)
W_pump ∝ N³      (power proportional to speed cubed)
W_pump = m_flow · ΔP / η
```

> **Source:** Affinity laws are implemented inside `TRANSFORM.Fluid.Machines.Pump_Controlled` (TRANSFORM library, not in ExaDigiT repo directly). The pump is instantiated in `PumpTrain.mo`:
> ```modelica
> TRANSFORM.Fluid.Machines.Pump_Controlled pump(
>     ...
>     use_port=true)
> ```
> Speed input N drives the pump characteristic. The cubic power law is a standard result from dimensional analysis of centrifugal machines.

### 10.5 Isolation Valve Flow Equation

```
m_flow = opening · m_flow_nominal · √(ΔP / ΔP_nominal)
```

> **Source:** `PumpTrain.mo`:
> ```modelica
> TRANSFORM.Fluid.Valves.ValveLinear valve(
>     dp_start=500,
>     dp_nominal=1000,
>     m_flow_nominal=port_a_nominal.m_flow)
> ```
> `ValveLinear` from TRANSFORM implements the linear valve equation. Flow is proportional to opening and square root of pressure drop ratio.

