## 13. Global Model Assumptions

All assumptions below were identified from component instantiation parameters, documentation strings, and media model choices across the analyzed files.

| Assumption | Evidence | Source |
|------------|----------|--------|
| Single-phase liquid water throughout | No two-phase media or boiling models used anywhere | All fluid component instantiations use `LinearWater` or custom water media |
| Incompressible approximation | Linear water media models with constant density | `Medium_inner = TRANSFORM.Media.Fluids.Water.LinearWaterHot_pT` in `CentralEnergyPlant/Models/v0.mo` |
| Lumped chip by default | nX=nY=nZ=1 | `chip_3D.mo` parameter defaults |
| Empirical UA table not generalizable | Table derived from Frontier CDU hardware | `CDU_HEX.mo` — hardcoded table values |
| York correlation within bounds only | `BoundsYorkCalc` component enforces limits | `YorkCalc.mo`: `Buildings.Fluid.HeatExchangers.CoolingTowers.Correlations.BoundsYorkCalc bou` |
| All CT towers see same ambient | Single Towb replicated to all towers | `CoolingTowerLoop/Models/v0.mo`: `Replicator replicator(nout=nCoolingTowers)` |
| No fouling or degradation | No fouling resistance parameters | Absent from all HX models |
| No solar/wind/humidity dynamics | Only Towb as environmental input | Only `RealInput Towb` in `coolingTower_Towb.mo` |
| Workload = heat load only | Q_flow only — no PUE overhead | `Cabinet/Models/v0.mo` only injects Q_flow |
| Parallel scaling approximation | N physical units → 1 simulated unit | `TRANSFORM.Fluid.Pipes.parallelFlow` used throughout |
| Constant cp for water | cp = 4184 J/kg·K | `YorkCalc.mo` documentation: *"h = cp(T-T₀), cp = 4184 J/(kg K)"* |
| Adiabatic chip ends | Adiabatic boundary on X and Y faces | `chip_3D.mo`: `T_infX1`, `T_infX2`, `T_infY1`, `T_infY2` all set to `Tamb` |

